cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MetaGráfica: a descriptive language for technical and scientific figures"
abstract: >
  MetaGráfica is a descriptive language for publication-quality 2D vector
  graphics. A figure is plain-text source — points, paths, parameterized
  structures, transformations, plots and mathematical typesetting — that the
  mg compiler turns into EPS, SVG or PDF, so it can be versioned, diffed,
  parameterized and regenerated. Created for the figures of scientific
  textbooks, it has been in use since 1988.
